    "work_basis": "Decode-step analytical operation and byte counts. Index projection uses two FLOPs per released indexer parameter; scan uses one multiply-add per query-head key element; top-k counts scored candidates. Attention uses absorbed MLA core arithmetic over semantic latent and rotary state; common per-step query and output absorption transforms are excluded. Main-cache traffic uses compressed semantic MLA state. Index-key traffic uses the independent typed storage scenario including per-token metadata. The HBM IndexShare handoff counts 21 top-k writes plus 78 attention reads for the supplied layer pattern; the zero-HBM-handoff upper bound removes only this HBM traffic and does not model SRAM movement. Allocator, scale metadata outside the typed index-key scenario, paging metadata, transaction amplification, distributed mapping, overlap, and utilization are excluded. Every-layer indexing is a same-geometry analytical counterfactual, not a GLM-5.1 deployment measurement.",
